(1.  A and C share the same formula: A[i][k] and C[i][j] land in the same set whenever k/4 == j/4, so reading A evicts C.) Tj
ET
0 g
0.15 g
BT
/F1 7.60 Tf
62.00 171.00 Td
(2.  The set only depends on row mod 8: row i and row i+8 own exactly the same 4 sets \(4*\(i+8\) = 4i + 32 = 4i mod 32\). B likewise.) Tj
ET
0 g
0.15 g
BT
/F1 7.60 Tf
62.00 154.00 Td
(3.  One matrix = 64 cache lines; the cache holds only 32 lines. A+B+C = 192 lines, the cache is 1/6 of that.) Tj
ET
0 g
0.15 g
BT
/F1 7.60 Tf
62.00 137.00 Td
(4.  Each row owns 4 consecutive sets, so the colour cycle repeats every 4 columns and row 8 looks exactly like row 0.) Tj
ET
0 g
0.15 g
BT
/F1 7.60 Tf
62.00 120.00 Td
(5.  buffer starts at int 768 \(line 192, sets 0..15\): it competes with the even rows of A and C.) Tj
